    "result_text": "The full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement \u2014 all rejection responses (400, 409, 429) returning an RFC7807 `application/problem+json` body with `type`, `title`, `status`, and `detail`, with HTTP status codes unchanged \u2014 is **already fully satisfied** by the codebase, and the test suite passes.\n\n**How it works.** All rejections funnel through a single `@ControllerAdvice` (`ExceptionControllerAdvice`). Its `detailBuild(...)` builds a Spring `ProblemDetail` populating all four required members (`status` via `ProblemDetail.forStatus`, `type`, `title`, `detail`), and every in-scope handler returns `ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>`. Spring MVC then serializes `ProblemDetail` with content type `application/problem+json` automatically.\n\n**Coverage verified.** Every rejection rule in the create pipeline throws an exception that maps to a problem+json handler:\n- **400** \u2014 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` (bean validation) and the `InvalidOwnerFieldException` hierarchy (telephone/address/postcode/email/registration-date).\n- **409** \u2014 the `OwnerConflictException` hierarchy (duplicate identity, city capacity, household duplicate).\n- **429** \u2014 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException`.\n\nI confirmed this empirically with a temporary probe test asserting `contentTypeCompatibleWith(\"application/problem+json\")` plus the presence of `type`/`title`/`status`/`detail` on live 400 (field-level), 409, and 429 responses \u2014 all passed. I then removed the probe, leaving the tree unchanged, and re-ran the suite: **BUILD SUCCESS** (`AcceptanceTest.coreRejectionIsProblemJson` green).\n\nNo production code changes were needed. One note for transparency: a malformed/unreadable JSON body currently returns **500** (the catch-all `Exception` handler intercepts `HttpMessageNotReadableException`), not 400 \u2014 but that is outside the stated scope (it isn't a 400/409/429, status codes are to stay unchanged, and the acceptance harness only sends well-formed JSON). I left it as-is; let me know if you'd like that path mapped to a 400 problem+json as well.",
